ukui-power-manager: lock the screen on the (timed) idle blank

Bug (verified on sheng): the "此时间段后关闭显示器" (idle) blank turns the panel
off but never locks — so with "唤醒屏幕时需要密码" (org.ukui.screensaver
close-activation-enabled) on, waking a timed-blank screen did NOT ask for the
password (whereas the power-key "关闭显示器" action does).

Root cause: PowerManagementDaemon/idle/idlenesswatcher.cpp's IdlenessWatchcer runs
its lock step as

    QProcess process;
    process.start("ukui-screensaver-command -b idle");   // <-- wrong
    process.waitForFinished();

but Qt's QProcess::start(const QString &program) does NOT split on spaces — it
tries to exec a file literally named "ukui-screensaver-command -b idle", which
does not exist, so the process fails to start (QProcess::FailedToStart) and the
lock never happens.  (The blank itself uses system("... kscreen-doctor --dpms
off"), which DOES go through a shell, so it works — hence "blanks but no lock".)

The shipped fix (tools/sheng-power-button-blank-fix.sh, PART 3) repoints that
program string to the no-space wrapper /usr/local/bin/sheng-idle-lock, which runs
`ukui-screensaver-command --lock` when close-activation-enabled is on (immediate
lock; `-b idle` only locked after a few seconds).  This is the equivalent source
change (pass program + args properly, and lock immediately):

--- a/PowerManagementDaemon/idle/idlenesswatcher.cpp
+++ b/PowerManagementDaemon/idle/idlenesswatcher.cpp
@@ (mTurnOffDisplayTimer timeout lambda, initIdleWatcher)
         turnOffDisplay();
         turnOffDisplaySignal(true);
 
         QProcess process;
-        process.start("ukui-screensaver-command -b idle");
+        // sheng: lock immediately (ask for password on wake) iff configured.
+        if (QGSettings("org.ukui.screensaver").get("close-activation-enabled").toBool())
+            process.start("ukui-screensaver-command", QStringList{ "--lock" });
         process.waitForFinished();
         mTurnOffDisplayTimer->stop();
     });
